<title>UK: Algeria's Skikda port reopens - port official.</title>
<headline>Algeria's Skikda port reopens - port official.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's Skikda port reopened on Wednesday with one oil tanker now loading and two other oil tankers due to berth later in the day, a port official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Seven oil tankers were still waiting outside the port, the official said, bringing to 10 the number delayed by the bad weather that had shut Skikda for most of the last two weeks.</p>
<p>The weather forecast had improved, the official said.</p>
<p>Naphtha traders said four tankers originally set to hold 55,000 to 60,000 tonnes were delayed by the bad weather.</p>
<p>A methane carrier was scheduled to berth on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- John Hanley, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8185</p>
</text>
